  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "A particle moves with a constant velocity of $(6i+2j)\\,\\text{cm/s}.$ If its initial position is ${r}_{0}=(3i-5j)\\,\\text{cm},$ find its position vector $r$ after $5$ seconds.\n\n$r=(${{field-1}}  \n$i\\,\\,+$  \n{{field-2}}  \n$j)\\text{cm}$",
  "worked_solution": "When a particle (or object) moves with constant velocity $u,$ the position vector at time $t$ is given by the equation\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut,\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position vector.\n\nIn this case,\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=3i-5j,\\,u=6i+2j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t=5\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & ={r}_{0}+ut \\\\  & =(3i-5j)+(6i+2j)(5) \\\\  & =3i-5j+30i+10j \\\\  & =(\\,33\\,i+5\\,j)\\,\\text{cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
